Good catch 👍—this is a version/behavior difference in Power Apps.

The error:

'Result' isn't recognized

happens because your Split() output column is not named Result in your environment.


---

✅ SIMPLE FIX (USE Index)

Instead of First(...).Result, use:

"Welcome " & Index(Split(User().FullName, " "), 1).Value & "!"


---

🧠 WHY THIS WORKS

Split() returns a table

In newer Power Apps versions, the column is Value, not Result

Index(...,1) safely gets the first word



---

🧩 ALTERNATIVE (CHECK YOUR COLUMN NAME)

If you want to confirm, temporarily use:

First(Split(User().FullName, " "))

👉 It will show something like:

{ Value: "King" }

or

{ Result: "King" }


---

🎯 MOST COMPATIBLE VERSION (SAFE)

If you want something that works in almost all environments:

"Welcome " & Left(User().FullName, Find(" ", User().FullName & " ") - 1) & "!"


---

🎉 RESULT

✔ No error
✔ Shows first name only
✔ Works across versions


---

👍 BONUS

If you want fallback (in case no space in name):

"Welcome " & 
If(
    IsError(Find(" ", User().FullName)),
    User().FullName,
    Left(User().FullName, Find(" ", User().FullName) - 1)
) 
& "!"


